{"The Delete method creates a local log variable with additional context values but then passes the base d.Log to the context instead of the enriched log variable, causing log messages to miss contextual information": 0.9725549221038818, "In DeleteCollection, the legacy goroutine calls recordStorageDuration() instead of recordLegacyDuration(), causing metrics for legacy DeleteCollection operations to be incorrectly recorded as storage operations": 0.9951750040054321, "The success path of Delete uses 'name' as the third parameter instead of 'options.Kind', breaking metric aggregation since metrics labels for successful Delete operations will have object names instead of kinds": 0.9747247695922852, "All async goroutines use the parent context which may already be canceled or have a deadline exceeded by the time the goroutine executes, causing legacy writes to fail immediately if the parent request completes before the goroutine executes": 0.8093812465667725, "When Storage operations fail in Create (line 45) and Update (line 129), the code calls recordLegacyDuration() instead of recordStorageDuration(), causing storage error metrics to be recorded as legacy metrics": 0.9928227066993713, "In the Update method goroutine, defer cancel() is placed after startLegacy assignment instead of immediately after creating the context, potentially holding timer resources slightly longer than necessary": 0.22037111222743988}